 "about_text": "Pace's Los Angeles gallery is the West Coast flagship of Pace Gallery, an international gallery founded by Arne Glimcher in Boston in 1960. Pace has had a presence in California for six decades and opened this dedicated LA space, on La Brea Avenue, in 2022. As part of Pace's global program, the Los Angeles gallery presents an intergenerational mix of contemporary and modern artists, connecting newer voices with long-represented figures and legacy estates. The gallery's program reflects Pace's broader emphasis on dialogue between contemporary practice and twentieth-century art, including strong historical ties to the Light and Space movement associated with Southern California.",
